# The damped harmonic oscillator
# A mass on a spring with a damper: m x'' + c x' + k x = 0. With weak
# damping it rings just below the frequency sqrt(k/m) while its amplitude
# decays as exp(-c t / 2m).
x'=v
v'=-(k*x+c*v)/m
par m=1,k=1,c=0.2
init x=1,v=0
@ total=50,dt=0.01,meth=rungekutta
@ xp=t,yp=x,xlo=0,xhi=50,ylo=-1,yhi=1
done
